  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Three dice are rolled and the sum of the numbers is recorded. Find the probability that the result is less than 17.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{53}{54}$.\n\nSubtract the probability of a sum of 17 or 18 from 1.",
      "worked": "There are $6^3=216$ equally likely ordered outcomes. A sum of 17 occurs for $(5,6,6)$, $(6,5,6)$ and $(6,6,5)$; a sum of 18 occurs only for $(6,6,6)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(S\\ge17)&=\\frac{4}{216}\\\\\\Pr(S<17)&=1-\\frac{4}{216}\\\\\\Pr(S<17)&=\\frac{53}{54}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
